third_party/opus/BUILD.gn: compile in deep PLC (FARGAN/LPCNet-lite) and
OSCE (LACE/NoLACE, no BWE), arm64 only.

Chromium's `src/third_party/opus` already vendors every .c/.h file this
needs (verified against the real, exact revision webrtc's own DEPS pins for
src/third_party - see "Verified" below); it just never compiles them,
because Chromium's own use of libopus never asked for deep PLC or SILK
enhancement. This patch only adds `sources` entries, `include_dirs` and
`defines`; it does not touch, remove or reorder anything already there.

- `config("opus_config")`: arm64-only self-report defines
  (QAUDION_OPUS_DEEP_PLC=1, QAUDION_OPUS_OSCE=1) so
  modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/audio_decoder_opus.cc (P4b, a different
  GN target) can log what a given binary actually has compiled in, without
  duplicating the current_cpu check. This works because opus_config is
  already `public_configs` on the `opus` target (BUILD.gn:379 at this
  revision), so its defines propagate to every dependent, including
  modules/audio_coding:webrtc_opus.
- `config("opus_private_config")`: adds "src/dnn" to include_dirs (needed
  by every file below), and - nested inside the *existing* arm64-only
  `if (current_cpu == "arm64")` block, not a new one, since that is already
  exactly the scope the owner wants this limited to - `ENABLE_DEEP_PLC` and
  `ENABLE_OSCE`. Macro names are xiph/opus's own
  (configure.ac --enable-deep-plc/--enable-osce; CMakeLists.txt's OPUS_OSCE
  option), stable across releases, not repinned for 55513e81 specifically
  because that would need re-verifying configure.ac at the exact commit,
  which I could not fetch (see "Verified").
- `static_library("opus")`: after the existing arm sources block, adds (all
  arm64-only):
  - Deep PLC, xiph/opus's own DEEP_PLC_SOURCES (dnn/burg.c, freq.c,
    fargan.c, fargan_data.c, lpcnet_enc.c, lpcnet_plc.c, lpcnet_tables.c,
    nnet.c, nnet_default.c, plc_data.c, parse_lpcnet_weights.c, pitchdnn.c,
    pitchdnn_data.c) plus dnn/arm/nnet_neon.c (NEON kernels; no runtime
    dotprod dispatch - single ABI, arm64 only, per the owner's decision).
  - OSCE, xiph/opus's own OSCE_SOURCES (dnn/osce.c, osce_features.c,
    nndsp.c, lace_data.c, nolace_data.c) MINUS dnn/bbwenet_data.c: I
    grepped the actual vendored osce.c/osce_features.c/nndsp.c/
    osce_config.h/osce_structs.h at this exact revision for "bbwe" and got
    zero hits - OSCE-BWE (blind bandwidth extension) does not exist yet at
    opus upstream 55513e81, so there is no bbwenet_* symbol to link and no
    reason to fetch its weights. This also matches the pinned model tarball
    (opus-dnn-weights-160753e9, sha256
    160753e983198f29f1aae67c54caa0e30bd90f1ce916a52f15bdad2df8e35e58),
    which I listed directly: it contains fargan/lace/nolace/pitchdnn/plc
    _data.[ch] and nothing named bbwenet. OSCE-BWE is therefore not "spent
    but decided against" here, it is simply unavailable at this revision -
    worth knowing if OSCE-BWE is revisited on a later Opus roll.
  - The *_data.[ch] files themselves (fargan/plc/pitchdnn/lace/nolace) are
    not in this vendored tree - m150/fetch-opus-dnn-weights.sh (the
    pipeline's script) extracts them from the model tarball into
    third_party/opus/src/dnn before this patch's `sources` list can resolve
    them; the list above matches exactly what that script's
    `--wildcards 'dnn/*_data.[ch]'` produces for this tarball, checked
    against the tarball's own file listing, not the script's intent.

Deliberately not touched: OPUS_ARM_ASM/OPUS_ARM_MAY_HAVE_NEON (P4a's own
`config("opus_config")` addition is a *different*, non-conflicting set of
arm64-only defines from those already set in opus_private_config for
CELT/SILK's own ARM NEON code - no overlap, no override), and nothing in
`opus_test_config` or the `opus_sse41`/x86 paths, which the owner's "solo
arm64" decision does not touch.

Order: 5th in the series (m150/series), right after P8 (whose
qaudion_tuning.h is what P4b/P5 use once this patch's sources exist) and
before P4b (deep PLC / decoder complexity) and P5 (FEC floor / encoder
complexity), which both depend on QAUDION_OPUS_DEEP_PLC/QAUDION_OPUS_OSCE
being defined correctly here to produce a meaningful self-verification log.
Applies inside the *separate* src/third_party checkout
(`git -C src/third_party apply`), dir `third_party` in m150/series - this
is the only patch in the series that does.

Touches: third_party/opus/BUILD.gn only (path `opus/BUILD.gn` relative to
src/third_party).

Verified: unlike P8/P4b/P5, I could not reach chromium.googlesource.com
directly from this sandbox for most of this session (persistent 503s on
every subdomain, including from the owner's own Helsinki VPS, so this
looks like an upstream outage rather than a local restriction) - `git
apply --check`/symbol-checking this patch therefore first went through
guesswork based on the plan's own Appendix A. I then found that the VPS
*can* reach chromium.googlesource.com's git-over-HTTP endpoint even though
its web/gitiles browsing endpoint (the one `?format=TEXT` URLs use) 503s,
and used `git fetch --filter=blob:none --depth 1` + a sparse checkout of
`opus/` from `https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party`
at `7c92732938de0ef7e28f5da231994723f938f407` - the exact commit
webrtc-sdk/webrtc's own DEPS pins for `src/third_party` at
ba469aa2093ba950066258ca0a59a6fbd1295582 (DEPS line 88-89, read from the
GitHub mirror). That gave me the real, current third_party/opus/BUILD.gn
(sha256 152fdf2929b24444643c9bc91471ecd6b927792c63df8c770c9d3aa5cb0e1c62)
and README.chromium (confirms "Revision: 55513e81d8f606bd75d0ff773d2144e
5f2a732f5", i.e. the opus upstream commit the plan's "55513e81" refers to),
and a full `git ls-tree` of third_party/opus/src/dnn confirming every
source file this patch references exists there already (and that no
*_data.[ch] or bbwenet file of any kind does). `git apply --check` and a
real apply of the diff above are clean against that exact file, and the
resulting file is byte-identical (modulo CRLF from a Windows git checkout)
to the one I hand-edited. The plan's own line-number references for this
file (arm block ending ~:107, arm sources block ending ~:410-435) matched
what I found almost exactly, which is a good sign the plan's original
research (done with real access before that scratch dir was deleted) was
accurate here too.

Not verified: `clang -fsyntax-only` on the newly-referenced dnn/*.c files
themselves (P4a only changes BUILD.gn, not any .c/.h content, so this is a
build-graph change, not a source change - the actual compile would need
the *_data.[ch] weight files the pipeline extracts, which I have locally
from the same tarball but did not attempt to cross-compile against). I did
grep the three logic files' own #includes (osce.c, osce_features.c,
nndsp.c all just want arch.h/config.h/float_cast.h/os_support.h/pitch.h/
stack_alloc.h from src/celt - already in include_dirs - and freq.h/nndsp.h/
nnet.h/osce.h/osce_features.h from src/dnn, which this patch adds to
include_dirs) so nothing in the sources list should be missing an include
path.

diff --git a/opus/BUILD.gn b/opus/BUILD.gn
index 1b75504..2d96764 100644
--- a/opus/BUILD.gn
+++ b/opus/BUILD.gn
@@ -12,6 +12,19 @@ use_opus_x86_optimization = current_cpu == "x86" || current_cpu == "x64"
 
 config("opus_config") {
   include_dirs = [ "src/include" ]
+
+  # Q-Audion (M150 hardening, P4a): arm64-only, self-report defines so
+  # dependents outside this target (webrtc's
+  # modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/audio_decoder_opus.cc, P4b) can log
+  # what this specific binary was actually built with, without duplicating
+  # the current_cpu check. Safe to read from a dependent because this
+  # config is `public_configs` below.
+  if (current_cpu == "arm64") {
+    defines = [
+      "QAUDION_OPUS_DEEP_PLC=1",
+      "QAUDION_OPUS_OSCE=1",
+    ]
+  }
 }
 
 config("opus_private_config") {
@@ -32,6 +45,7 @@ config("opus_private_config") {
     "src/silk",
     "src/silk/fixed",
     "src/silk/float",
+    "src/dnn",
   ]
 
   cflags = []
@@ -103,6 +117,22 @@ config("opus_private_config") {
 
     if (current_cpu == "arm64") {
       defines += [ "OPUS_ARM_PRESUME_AARCH64_NEON_INTR" ]
+
+      # Q-Audion (M150 hardening, P4a): deep PLC (FARGAN + the LPCNet-lite
+      # pieces it needs) and OSCE (LACE/NoLACE only - no OSCE_BWE; osce.c /
+      # osce_features.c at this exact revision (opus upstream 55513e81,
+      # per third_party/opus/README.chromium) have no bbwenet_* symbol at
+      # all - grepped the actual vendored files, not assumed - so nothing
+      # here needs dnn/bbwenet_data.c, which the pinned model tarball
+      # (opus-dnn-weights-160753e9, sha256
+      # 160753e983198f29f1aae67c54caa0e30bd90f1ce916a52f15bdad2df8e35e58)
+      # does not contain anyway). Nested in the existing arm64-only branch,
+      # not a new if-block, because that is already exactly the scope the
+      # owner wants this in (solo arm64: Android arm64-v8a, iOS device +
+      # simulator arm64). Macro names are xiph/opus's own
+      # (configure.ac: --enable-deep-plc/--enable-osce; CMakeLists.txt:
+      # OPUS_OSCE) and stable across releases.
+      defines += [ "ENABLE_DEEP_PLC", "ENABLE_OSCE" ]
     }
   }
 }
@@ -432,6 +462,40 @@ static_library("opus") {
       "src/silk/arm/macros_armv5e.h",
     ]
   }
+
+  if (current_cpu == "arm64") {
+    sources += [
+      # Deep PLC: FARGAN + the LPCNet-lite pieces it needs. File list is
+      # xiph/opus's own DEEP_PLC_SOURCES (lpcnet_sources.mk); every file
+      # below is already vendored at this revision (opus upstream
+      # 55513e81), just not referenced by this BUILD.gn yet.
+      "src/dnn/burg.c",
+      "src/dnn/freq.c",
+      "src/dnn/fargan.c",
+      "src/dnn/fargan_data.c",
+      "src/dnn/lpcnet_enc.c",
+      "src/dnn/lpcnet_plc.c",
+      "src/dnn/lpcnet_tables.c",
+      "src/dnn/nnet.c",
+      "src/dnn/nnet_default.c",
+      "src/dnn/plc_data.c",
+      "src/dnn/parse_lpcnet_weights.c",
+      "src/dnn/pitchdnn.c",
+      "src/dnn/pitchdnn_data.c",
+      "src/dnn/arm/nnet_neon.c",
+
+      # OSCE: LACE/NoLACE only, no OSCE_BWE (see opus_private_config above).
+      # File list is xiph/opus's own OSCE_SOURCES (lpcnet_sources.mk) minus
+      # dnn/bbwenet_data.c, which is neither referenced by osce.c /
+      # osce_features.c at this revision nor present in the pinned model
+      # tarball.
+      "src/dnn/osce.c",
+      "src/dnn/osce_features.c",
+      "src/dnn/nndsp.c",
+      "src/dnn/lace_data.c",
+      "src/dnn/nolace_data.c",
+    ]
+  }
 }
 
